libdisplay-info reads EDID and DisplayID data from monitors (names, supported modes,
colorimetry). wlroots uses it to identify outputs. Installs libdisplay-info, headers,
libdisplay-info.pc and the di-edid-decode tool under /usr/local.
The source is the Ubuntu archive's copy of the upstream release tarball 
upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info
